Package: saddlepoint
Title: A Framework for the Saddlepoint Approximation with CGF Operations
Version: 0.9.0
Date: 2026-07-16
Authors@R: c(
    person("Godrick", "Oketch", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "godrick@berkeley.edu"),
    person(c("Rachel", "M."), "Fewster", role = c("aut")),
    person("Jesse", "Goodman", role = c("aut")))
Maintainer: Godrick Oketch <godrick@berkeley.edu>
Author: Godrick Oketch [aut, cre],
    Rachel M. Fewster [aut],
    Jesse Goodman [aut]
Description: Tools for saddlepoint approximations built around composable
    cumulant generating function (CGF) objects. Provides CGFs for common
    distributions, operators to combine CGFs (i.i.d. replication, sums, linear
    maps, random sums and tilts), and routines for saddlepoint likelihood
    inference including maximum likelihood estimation. Uses RTMB for automatic
    differentiation where derivatives are required. The framework is described
    in Oketch, Fewster and Goodman (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2607.17464>.
